# The epilogue week at a safehouse (docs/EPILOGUE.md): the world's outcome, who was there and this
# player's route are kept apart. The first true variant replaces the plain line. {resident} is the
# house's own seeded name, never one from the lore.

conv epilogue.occupant.greet
for occupant
when epilogue
greet
prio reaction
voice haven

node start
  say? was:every_name :: "You were at the table when the names were read. I saw you. Sit, there's soup. Real soup."
  say? cure_held:bastion :: "The cure came in a crate with a number on it. We're on a list for it. Everyone's on a list now."
  say? cure_held:everyone :: "Somebody walked it out to every house. Mrs {resident} asked who to thank, and nobody would say."
  say? ending:every_name=every_name :: "They read every name at supper. Even the crossed ones. Mrs {resident} cried, then went to bed early."
  say "The loudspeakers say processing at the checkpoints. Nobody's gone up yet. Nobody quite believes it."

conv epilogue.occupant.route
for occupant
when epilogue & route:bastion
topic "Tell them you stood with Bastion."
prio reaction
once
voice haven

node start
  say "I know. Everyone knows. Don't expect soup. ...There's soup. Don't expect it, that's all."
  > @back "Something else." -> hub
